  "description": "drand-quicknet+metoffice-landobs-v1: the weather_value grammar \"<t>;<mslp>;<rh>;<vis>\" (tenths of a degree C, whole hPa, whole percent, decametres) and how a Land Observations row becomes one. bounds apply to each part after rounding. valid values carry their parts; every invalid value must be refused. from_row: each row is raw JSON text; read it with a parser that keeps each number's text (60.0 and 60 differ, exponents are refused, 1e400 in a field nobody reads is fine). A float-based JSON reader does not test the grammar. Every row is synthetic, made in the format the Met Office Weather DataHub documents for Land Observations; none is a real observation. The single-field cases change one field of the 2026-10-15T12:00Z row.",
